Spec: Pending application registration journal

Purpose:
  Atomically retain unapproved manifests and caller-scoped operation results across Broker restarts.

Owns:
  ./RegistrationStore.cs

References:
  /contracts/dotnet/LinkGate.Contracts/ManifestContract.sdd
  /docs/adr/0003-pending-registration.md
  /docs/adr/0009-windows-declaration-review.md
  ./JournalCapacity.sdd
  ./PendingGrants.sdd
  ./SecureAuthority.sdd

Must:
  Migrate schema seven to eight atomically, preserving local access while adding empty connection/attachment journals and active-flow indexes.
  Keep schema-seven local visitor grants empty on migration; existing declaration and publisher approvals do not invent local access.
  Store normalized pending declarations and successful operation results in one SQLite immediate transaction with full synchronization.
  Deduplicate by OS-derived caller scope and operation UUID; compare canonical method and parameter digests without request IDs.
  Return the original success for matching retries, conflict for different parameters and unknown for another caller.
  Retain all results without eviction in this milestone; cap per-caller operations at `500000`, total at `1000000` and registrations at `1024`.
  Reject linked state paths, restrict state directory to the current user and SYSTEM and use parameterized SQL.
  Fail closed on storage errors or unknown schema versions; never grant network access from registration.
  Migrate schemas `1` through `7` atomically to `8`, preserving declarations/results and validating reservations before commit.
  Initialize legacy state without invented trust, grants or opens; reject missing current-schema storage rather than recreating it.
  Initialize schema-five authority epochs from existing decision versions, preserving both active and already invalid grant stamps.
  Increment pending revision only for a changed declaration; preserve approved state and never reapply an old registration operation.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Verify atomic registration, persistent retries, isolation and failure rollback.
